<title>PHILIPPINES: San Miguel sees beer sales rise.</title>
<headline>San Miguel sees beer sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>San Miguel Corp said on Monday it expects a sharp rise in beer sales in the second half of the year as a result of price cuts last month.</p>
<p>&quot;We're aiming at 20 percent growth in the second semester and we're on our way,&quot; Val Tan, marketing manager of its subsidiary San Miguel Brewing Philippines, told reporters.  </p>
<p>Last month, San Miguel cut prices by one peso a bottle.</p>
<p>In 1996, the company sold a total of 150 million cases of beer. It gave no figure for the first half of this year.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841 8914</p>
</text>
